From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] addons: ship our skin and the speech and 3D add-ons enabled

The image carries skin.estuary.allolive, script.module.subtitlespeech.allolive
(the voice activity model the subtitle realignment listens with) and
service.shutter3d.allolive (active 3D glasses) in Kodi's own add-ons, put
there by their packages from the allolive repository's releases. Kodi adds
an add-on it finds there disabled unless the manifest names it: listed as
optional, they start enabled, can be disabled, and update from the
repository like the others.

Estuary stays Kodi's default skin, the one it falls back to when a skin
fails to load; the build starts a new profile on ours.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
diff --git a/system/addon-manifest.xml b/system/addon-manifest.xml
index 35b72b8..266cfa8 100644
--- a/system/addon-manifest.xml
+++ b/system/addon-manifest.xml
@@ -38,6 +38,9 @@
   <addon>metadata.tvshows.themoviedb.org.python</addon>
   <addon>repository.xbmc.org</addon>
   <addon optional="true">repository.allolive</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">script.module.subtitlespeech.allolive</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">service.shutter3d.allolive</addon>
+  <addon optional="true">skin.estuary.allolive</addon>
   <addon>resource.images.weathericons.default</addon>
   <addon>resource.language.en_gb</addon>
   <addon>resource.uisounds.kodi</addon>
